{% comment %}
  What the picker CALLS this visitor's location — the words printed in the
  header's trigger, in the mobile menu's row, and in the drawer's heading.

  It is the country's name where the store lists that country by name, and
  "Rest of world" where it does not. The bare domain's market carries every
  country the eleven markets do not, and Shopify hands the theme that
  market's PRIMARY country as the current one — "Bermuda", which named a
  place nobody was and told a visitor nothing about what they were being
  charged. The market is the honest answer there: one currency, one set of
  prices, one shipping zone, and its name in the picker's own list is
  "Rest of world" (the owner's word, 9 Sep 2026). The country is still
  said, where it is known, on the Rest of world ROW inside the drawer —
  "Rest of world · India" — which is where somebody checks.

  Which countries are named is `settings.location_named_countries`, read
  here exactly as snippets/location-list.liquid reads it: the two must
  agree, or the bar would name a country the list files under Rest of
  world. `docs/spikes/location-picker.mjs` pins them together.

  Renders nothing but the words, so it can sit inside any element.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign named_raw = settings.location_named_countries | default: '' | upcase | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', ''
  assign named = named_raw | split: ','
  if named_raw == '' or named contains localization.country.iso_code
    echo localization.country.name
  else
    echo 'localization.rest_of_world' | t
  endif
-%}
